* GKR Protocol
** Foundations
*** Interactive proofs (IP = PSPACE)
*** Sum-check protocol
**** v-variate polynomial g
**** v rounds, soundness error v*d / |F|
**** One final oracle query
*** Multilinear extension (MLE)
**** Unique multilinear polynomial extending f
**** Lagrange basis construction
**** Schwartz-Zippel: one point identifies the table

** GKR core
*** Layered arithmetic circuits
**** D layers, 2^m gates per layer
**** Layer 0 = output, layer D = inputs
*** Gate value polynomials
**** V_i: gate values at layer i
**** V-tilde_i: MLE of V_i
*** Wiring predicates
**** A_i, M_i: MLE of gate connectivity
*** Fundamental recurrence
**** V-tilde_i(z) = sum over gate pairs in layer i+1
**** One sum-check instance per layer
**** Line restriction: 2 claims => 1 claim
*** Final check: V evaluates the input MLE directly

** Complexity
*** Prover: O(S log S)
*** Verifier: O(n + D polylog S)
*** Communication: O(D log S) field elements
*** Log-space uniform: verifier O(n polylog n)

** Zero-knowledge variant
*** Mask each round polynomial with r_j
*** Constraint r_j(0) + r_j(1) = 0 preserves the sum
*** Soundness unchanged

** Applications
*** Theory: #P in IP, NC in IP
*** Transparent zkSNARKs (Spartan, Hyrax)
*** GKR-based SNARKs (Libra)
*** Ingredient in ZK-STARKs
*** Delegated ML inference, genomic matching
@endmindmap
